course: dictionary
lesson: 2690
title: Words for helpers and experts
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can name a job, and the words around it can show you what that job is. «A chatbot can sound like a doctor, a dietician, a counsellor or even a famous person who has died, but it is none of them.» The sentence lists people who give help, so a dietician must be some kind of helper too.
explain: Look at the other names in that list. A doctor looks after your body when you are ill, and a counsellor helps you talk about your feelings and problems. A dietician is the food and eating expert in the list, so the three words are different kinds of experts.
explain: Use the check to test your meaning. Put it into the sentence: «A chatbot can sound like a health expert who gives advice about food and eating.» It still makes sense, so you have understood dietician.
fact: A dietician is a trained health expert who gives advice about food and eating.
fact: A dietician may help someone with diabetes, with allergies, or who needs to gain or lose weight.
fact: «See a dietician» means visit a food and eating expert for advice.
fact: Hospitals and schools sometimes have a «hospital dietician» on their team.
fact: Dietician is a noun, so you can have one dietician or many dieticians.
exercise: «A chatbot can sound like a doctor, a dietician, a counsellor or even a famous person who has died, but it is none of them.» What is a dietician? | A teacher who teaches swimming | *A trained health expert who gives advice about food and eating | A driver who delivers food to shops | A person who runs a sweet shop
exercise: Which person would most likely see a dietician? | A person who is lost in a forest | A person who wants to learn the piano | A person who needs a new pair of shoes | *A person with allergies who needs help planning meals
exercise: Find and copy the word from the sentence that names a person who helps you with feelings and problems. | doctor | famous | *counsellor | chatbot
test: Which word means a trained health expert who gives advice about food and eating? | chatbot | doctor | counsellor | *dietician
test: What does «see a dietician» mean? | Buy a new dietician from a shop | *Visit a food and eating expert for advice | Watch a film about dieting | Look up a word in a dictionary
exam: Which sentence uses dietician correctly? | Dietician is the colour of the sky | *The hospital dietician helped Mia plan healthy meals after her illness | The dietician flew a kite in the park | I dietician my dinner every night
